The '''1996-97 season''' was the 103rd season of competitive football by [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]].

Celtic finished the League second to [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] same as the previous season; despite getting more points than their rivals against the rest of the teams in the league, they lost all four Old Firm derbies to end five points off the Govan club, equaling Celtic's 1966-74 record of [[Nine in a row|nine-in-a-row]] league titles.

Manager and former player [[Tommy Burns (footballer)|Tommy Burns]] was sacked shortly after losing the [[1996–97 Scottish Cup#Semi-finals|Scottish Cup semi-final]] to [[Falkirk F.C.|Falkirk]],{{Citation needed|date=June 2025}} and [[Billy Stark]] finished the season as caretaker.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kyle |first=Gregor |date=2014-05-23 |title=In pictures: The complete list of Celtic managers |url=http://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/gallery/3594386 |access-date=2025-06-10 |website=Daily Record |language=en}}</ref> It was the second season in a row with no major honours for the Glasgow club, and the ninth in a row in which they failed to win the League.

